---js
{
  layout: "layouts/interior.njk",
  pageJs: "service",
  pagination: { data: "services", size: 1, alias: "svc", addAllPagesToCollections: true },
  permalink: "/services/{{ svc.slug }}/",
  cta: { inline: true },
  eleventyComputed: {
    title: (data) => data.svc.name,
    description: (data) => data.svc.promise,
    // The header band (layouts/interior.njk). Breadcrumbs carry the
    // service's category, which is an anchor on /services/.
    head: (data) => {
      const s = data.svc;
      const cat = {
        web: { label: "Websites", id: "websites" },
        care: { label: "Care & visibility", id: "care-visibility" },
        brand: { label: "Branding & design", id: "branding-design" },
        print: { label: "Print & apparel", id: "print-apparel" },
      }[s.family];
      const brand = s.family === "brand";
      // The service's own light: the same hue its card carries on /services/
      // (components/sv-card.njk hueFor): its category's base hue, stepped
      // down 15 degrees per place in that category.
      const base = { web: 285, care: 175, brand: 100, print: 40 }[s.family];
      const idx = data.services.filter((x) => x.family === s.family).findIndex((x) => x.slug === s.slug);
      return {
        hue: base - idx * 15,
        icon: s.icon,
        back: { label: "Back to services", url: "/services/" },
        crumbs: [
          { label: "Services", url: "/services/" },
          { label: cat.label, url: `/services/#${cat.id}` },
          { label: s.name },
        ],
        heading: s.name,
        lede: s.promise,
        actions: [
          { label: "Start a project", url: brand ? `/contact/?service=${s.slug}` : "/contact/" },
          brand
            ? { label: "See the price list", url: "/pricing/#brand-and-design" }
            : { label: "See packages", url: "/packages/" },
        ],
      };
    },
  },
}
---
{#
  ONE SERVICE: what it costs, what it is, how it gets made.
    1. the price, in the shape the service is sold in:
         levels  - a chart whose column heads are the choice. A lit column
                   (the site's bar across its top) glides to the level chosen
                   or pointed at, and a package row beneath lights the
                   packages that include that level. Business cards also
                   stand the card itself in the key light: ALVSolutions' own
                   card, live in the identity, turning over to its back;
         flat    - one price strip; on the branding pages, the work that
                   service produces (brand/proof.njk), then the logo ladder
                   (the key light glides along it, the bar rests under
                   where this service stands);
         package - the three packages on one floor line, the bar gliding;
         care    - the two plans, the key resting on the recommended one;
         soon    - a notice with its light off;
    2. what it is, and what you get: the case set large, its words lighting
       in order, then the detail as beats on a rail that fills with light;
       beside them, a sheet whose lit ticks come on in order;
    3. how it gets made: the homepage's scroll-lit line, shared;
    4. questions, one open at a time, the open one lit along its edge;
    5. often bought with this: service cards, their spotlight;
    6. the close.
  Every figure is read from _data. Motion lives in scripts/service.ts; the
  page is complete without it.
#}
{%- from "components/sv-card.njk" import card, hueFor with context %}
{%- from "components/identity.njk" import lockup %}
{%- set p = svc.pricing %}
{%- set brand = svc.family == "brand" %}
{%- set startUrl = ("/contact/?service=" + svc.slug) if (brand or svc.slug == "business-cards") else "/contact/" %}
{%- set myHue = hueFor(svc) | trim %}

{#- How one level of a service sits in each package, from that level's own
    `addon` block: included outright, one of a package's picks, or added on
    at its class price. A package that includes it gets the site's lit bar
    beneath it. -#}
{%- macro fitLevel(a) -%}
{%- if a -%}
{%- set incl = a.includedIn or [] -%}
{%- set paid = a.packages or [] -%}
{%- set classLC = (a.class or "") | lower -%}
{%- set key = "power" if a.class == "Power feature" else "pages" -%}
<ul class="sd-fit">
  {%- for pt in packages.tiers %}
  {%- set own = pt.slug in incl %}
  {%- set pick = pt.slug in paid %}
  {%- set n = (pt.picks[key] if pt.picks else 0) %}
  <li class="sd-fit-slot{% if own or pick %} is-in{% endif %}">
    <span class="sd-fit-pkg">{{ pt.name }}</span>
    <span class="sd-fit-what">
      {%- if own %}Included
      {%- elif pick %}{% if n > 1 %}One of its {{ n }} {{ classLC }} picks{% else %}Its {{ classLC }} pick{% endif %}
      {%- elif a.price %}Add for {{ a.price | price | safe }}
      {%- else %}Not included{% endif -%}
    </span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- The same row, read from a package's own facts (packages.json `has`). -#}
{%- macro fitHas(key) -%}
<ul class="sd-fit">
  {%- for pt in packages.tiers %}
  {%- set v = pt.has[key] %}
  <li class="sd-fit-slot{% if v %} is-in{% endif %}">
    <span class="sd-fit-pkg">{{ pt.name }}</span>
    <span class="sd-fit-what">{% if v === true %}Included{% elif v %}{{ v }}{% else %}Add it on its own{% endif %}</span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- ALVSolutions' own business card, set live in the identity: the same
    treatment a client's card gets, in the client's brand. `face` is split
    (the basic card's one face), mark (premium front) or back. -#}
{%- macro bcFace(face) -%}
{%- if face == "split" %}
<div class="sd-bc-face sd-bc-split">
  {{ lockup("card", "sd-bc-wm") }}
  <div class="sd-bc-who">
    <b>Sergio Alvarez</b>
    <span class="sd-bc-role">Founder</span>
    <span>{{ site.email }}</span>
    <span>alvsolutions.co</span>
    <span>{{ site.city }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{%- elif face == "mark" %}
<div class="sd-bc-face sd-bc-mark">
  <span class="sd-bc-glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {{ lockup("card", "sd-bc-wm") }}
  <i class="sd-bc-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
  <span class="sd-bc-tag">Professional business websites</span>
</div>
{%- else %}
<div class="sd-bc-face sd-bc-back">
  <img class="sd-bc-qr" src="/assets/showcase/alv-connect-qr.svg" alt="" width="41" height="41" />
  <div class="sd-bc-who">
    <b>Sergio Alvarez</b>
    <span class="sd-bc-role">Founder, ALVSolutions</span>
    <span>{{ site.email }}</span>
    <span>alvsolutions.co</span>
    <span>{{ site.city }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}


{#- ══════════════ 1. THE PRICE ══════════════ #}
{%- if p.kind == "levels" %}
{%- set L = p.levels %}
{%- set shotFlags = [] %}
{%- for l in L %}{% if l.shot %}{% set _ = shotFlags.push(1) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{%- set hasShots = shotFlags.length > 0 %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec sd-sec--first" id="price" aria-labelledby="price-h">
  <div class="sd-head">
    <h2 id="price-h" class="int-h2">{{ p.heading or "Two levels, and the rule for each." }}</h2>
    <p class="int-lede">Choose the one closest to your job. The rows below are what decides it, so the price is never a guess.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="sd-lv{% if hasShots %} sd-lv--shots{% endif %}" data-lv style="--n: {{ L.length }}">
    {%- if hasShots %}
    {#- The card itself, standing in the key light. Only the chosen level's
        card shows; the premium one turns over to its back. #}
    <div class="sd-stage" data-stage>
      <span class="key-cone" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {%- for l in L %}
      {%- if l.shot %}
      {%- set two = l.shot.faces.length > 1 %}
      <figure class="sd-bc" data-for="{{ loop.index0 }}">
        <div class="sd-bc-tilt">
          <div class="sd-bc-card">
            <div class="sd-bc-side sd-bc-side--front" role="img" aria-label="{{ l.label }} card, front: {{ 'the ALVSolutions wordmark on its own, with a lit bar beneath it' if two else 'the ALVSolutions wordmark, then name, role, email, website and city' }}.">
              {{ bcFace("mark" if two else "split") }}
            </div>
            {%- if two %}
            <div class="sd-bc-side sd-bc-side--back" role="img" aria-label="{{ l.label }} card, back: a QR code to the ALVSolutions contact page beside name, role, email, website and city." aria-hidden="true">
              {{ bcFace("back") }}
            </div>
            {%- endif %}
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="sd-bc-shadow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <figcaption class="sd-bc-cap">
          {%- if two %}
          <button class="sd-bc-flip" type="button" aria-pressed="false">
            <svg class="int-ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-refresh"/></svg><span>Show the back</span>
          </button>
          {%- endif %}
          <span>{{ "Front and back. The logo on its own, then your details." if two else "One face: the logo, your name and how to reach you." }} This is my own card, in the treatment your business gets.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}

    <div class="sd-lv-main">
      <div class="sd-chart-wrap">
        <div class="sd-chart">
          <span class="sd-slab" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <table class="sd-tbl">
            <caption class="alv-sr-only">What decides the price of {{ p.cmpName or (svc.name | lower) }}</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col"><span class="alv-sr-only">What decides it</span></th>
                {%- for l in L %}
                <th scope="col" data-col="{{ loop.index0 }}">
                  <label class="sd-pick">
                    <input class="sd-pick-in" id="lv-{{ loop.index0 }}" type="radio" name="level" value="{{ l.label | lower }}"{% if loop.first %} checked{% endif %} />
                    <span class="sd-pick-name">{{ l.label }}</span>
                    <span class="sd-pick-price">{{ l.price | price | safe }}</span>
                  </label>
                </th>
                {%- endfor %}
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {%- for f in p.factors %}
              <tr{% if f.example %} class="is-eg"{% endif %}>
                <th scope="row">{{ f.label }}</th>
                {%- for v in f.values %}
                <td data-col="{{ loop.index0 }}">
                  {%- if v === true %}<svg class="int-ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span class="alv-sr-only">Included</span>
                  {%- elif v === false %}<span class="int-cmp-dash" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="alv-sr-only">Not included</span>
                  {%- else %}{{ v }}{% endif -%}
                </td>
                {%- endfor %}
              </tr>
              {%- endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      {#- The chosen level, in a sentence, and where it sits in the packages. #}
      {%- for l in L %}
      <div class="sd-lv-sum" data-for="{{ loop.index0 }}">
        <p class="sd-lv-note"><b>{{ l.label }}, {{ l.price | price | safe }}.</b> {{ l.note }}</p>
        {%- if l.addon %}
        <p class="sd-fit-k">In a package</p>
        {{ fitLevel(l.addon) }}
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}

      {%- if p.extra %}
      <p class="sd-extra">
        <b class="sd-extra-p">{{ p.extra.price | money | safe }}</b>
        <span><span class="sd-extra-h">{{ p.extra.label }}</span> {{ p.extra.note }}</span>
      </p>
      {%- endif %}

      <div class="sd-act">
        <a class="alv-btn" href="{{ startUrl }}">Start a project</a>
        <a class="alv-tlink" href="/packages/">Compare packages</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- elif p.kind == "flat" %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec sd-sec--first" id="price" aria-labelledby="price-h">
  <div class="sd-head">
    <h2 id="price-h" class="int-h2">{{ p.heading or "One price, one time." }}</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="sd-flat" style="--hue: {{ myHue }}">
    <span class="key-cone" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <p class="sd-flat-price">
      {%- if p.from %}<span class="sv-pre">From</span> {% endif %}<b>{{ p.price | price | safe }}</b>
      <span class="sd-flat-unit">{{ p.unit or "quoted to the project" }}</span>
    </p>
    <div class="sd-flat-body">
      <p class="sd-flat-note">{{ p.note }}</p>
      {%- if p.extras %}
      <ul class="sd-flat-extras">
        {%- for x in p.extras %}
        <li><span>{{ x.label }}</span><b>+{{ x.price | price | safe }}</b></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
    <a class="alv-btn sd-flat-go" href="{{ startUrl }}">Start a project</a>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The work this service produces, straight after its price. -#}
{%- if brand %}{% include "brand/proof.njk" %}{% endif %}

{#- The branding ladder: which of the two logo services fits depends on how
    much of a brand you need. The bar rests under this page's rung; the key
    light glides along the rungs. -#}
{%- if brand %}
{%- set ladder = [
  { slug: "logo-design", q: "Need a logo?" },
  { slug: "brand-identity", q: "Need the whole brand?" }
] %}
{%- set onLadder = [] %}
{%- for r in ladder %}{% if r.slug == svc.slug %}{% set _ = onLadder.push(1) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec" aria-labelledby="ladder-h">
  <div class="sd-head">
    <h2 id="ladder-h" class="int-h2">{{ "How much of a brand do you need?" if onLadder.length else "No logo or brand style yet?" }}</h2>
    {%- if not onLadder.length %}<p class="int-lede">This work uses the branding you already have. If you do not have a logo yet, one of these comes first.</p>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <div class="sv-grid-wrap sd-ladder-wrap" data-spot=".sd-rung">
    <ol class="sd-ladder" style="--rungs: {{ ladder.length }}">
      {%- for r in ladder %}
      {%- set s = services | find("slug", r.slug) %}
      {%- set here = s.slug == svc.slug %}
      <li class="sd-rung{% if here %} is-here{% endif %}" style="--hue: {{ hueFor(s) | trim }}"{% if here %} data-rest{% endif %}>
        <a class="sd-rung-a" href="/services/{{ s.slug }}/"{% if here %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
          <span class="sd-rung-q">{{ r.q }}</span>
          <span class="sd-rung-name">{{ s.name }}</span>
          <span class="sd-rung-price">{% if s.pricing.from %}<span class="sv-pre">From</span> {% endif %}{{ s.pricing.price | price | safe }}</span>
          {%- if here %}<span class="sd-rung-here">You are here</span>{% endif %}
        </a>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <span class="sv-spot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{%- elif p.kind == "package" %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec sd-sec--first" id="price" aria-labelledby="price-h">
  <div class="sd-head">
    <h2 id="price-h" class="int-h2">Three packages, each one flat price.</h2>
    <p class="int-lede">Agreed before I start. Every build also carries a care plan, from {{ careplans.plans[0].price | price | safe }} a month, for hosting, security and edits.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="sv-tiers sd-tiers">
    {%- for t in packages.tiers %}
    <li><a class="sv-tier{% if t.recommended %} is-rec{% endif %}" href="/packages/#{{ t.slug }}">
      <span class="sv-tier-name">{{ t.name }}{% if t.recommended %} <span class="sd-tier-rec">Recommended</span>{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="sv-tier-price">{{ t.price | price | safe }}</span>
      <span class="sv-tier-pages">{{ t.has.pages }} pages</span>
      <span class="sd-tier-for">{{ t.for }}</span>
    </a></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  <div class="sd-act">
    <a class="alv-btn" href="{{ startUrl }}">Start a project</a>
    <a class="alv-tlink" href="/packages/#compare">Compare every feature</a>
  </div>
</section>

{%- elif p.kind == "care" %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec sd-sec--first" id="price" aria-labelledby="price-h">
  <div class="sd-head">
    <h2 id="price-h" class="int-h2">Two plans. Pick one.</h2>
    <p class="int-lede">{{ careplans.required }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="sv-grid-wrap" data-spot=".sd-plan">
    <ul class="sd-plans">
      {%- for pl in careplans.plans %}
      <li class="sd-plan{% if pl.recommended %} is-rec{% endif %}" style="--hue: {{ myHue - loop.index0 * 15 }}"{% if pl.recommended %} data-rest{% endif %}>
        <div class="sd-plan-top">
          <h3 class="sd-plan-name">{{ pl.name }}</h3>
          {%- if pl.recommended %}<span class="sd-plan-rec">Recommended</span>{% endif %}
        </div>
        <p class="sd-plan-price"><b>{{ pl.price | price | safe }}</b><span>a month</span></p>
        <p class="sd-plan-for">{{ pl.for }}</p>
        {%- if pl.builds %}<p class="sd-plan-builds">Everything in {{ pl.builds }}, plus:</p>{% endif %}
        <ul class="sd-list">
          {%- for i in pl.includes %}<li>{{ i }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <span class="sv-spot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>
  <p class="sd-note">{{ careplans.minimum }}</p>
</section>

{%- elif p.kind == "soon" %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec sd-sec--first" id="price" aria-labelledby="price-h">
  <div class="sd-soon">
    <i class="sd-soon-bar" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <div>
      <h2 id="price-h" class="sd-soon-h">Not open for orders yet.</h2>
      <p>The pricing is not settled, so there is no number here. I would rather say that than invent one and change it on you later.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="alv-tlink" href="/contact/">Ask me where it stands</a>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}


{#- ══════════════ 2. WHAT IT IS, AND WHAT YOU GET ══════════════ #}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec sd-story" aria-labelledby="about-h" style="--hue: {{ myHue }}">
  <h2 id="about-h" class="alv-sr-only">About {{ svc.name }}</h2>
  {#- The case: the first paragraph, its words lit in order by a pass of
      light the first time it is reached. -#}
  <div class="sd-about">
   <div class="sd-main">
    <p class="sd-lead" data-lead>{{ svc.intro[0] }}</p>
    {#- The rest, one beat each. The first sentence of a beat is its point,
        in the display face; what follows is the detail. -#}
    <div class="sd-beats">
      {%- for para in svc.intro %}
      {%- if not loop.first %}
      {%- set parts = para.split(". ") %}
      {%- set lead = parts[0] + ("." if parts.length > 1 else "") %}
      <div class="sd-beat" data-beat>
        <p><span class="sd-beat-lead">{{ lead }}</span>{% if parts.length > 1 %} <span class="sd-beat-rest">{{ parts.slice(1).join(". ") }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
   </div>
    <div class="sd-get" data-get>
      <h3 class="sd-get-h">{{ svc.getHeading or "What you get" }}</h3>
      <ul class="sd-list sd-list--lit">
        {%- for i in svc.includes %}
        <li style="--d: {{ loop.index0 }}">{{ i }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- if not svc.soon %}
      <div class="sd-get-foot">
        <h4 class="sd-fact-h">Turnaround</h4>
        <p>
          {%- if svc.turnaroundNote %}{{ svc.turnaroundNote | safe }}
          {%- else %}{%- set _rg = standalone | byGroup("project-extras") %}{%- set _rush = _rg.items | find("name", "Rush delivery") %}Typically <b>{{ site.turnaround }}</b> after the required content is received, depending on complexity. Need it sooner? <a class="alv-tlink" href="/packages/#extras">Rush delivery</a> is listed at {{ _rush.price | money | safe }}, and I quote the exact figure first.{% endif -%}
        </p>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if svc.packageKey or svc.callout %}
  <div class="sd-facts">
    {%- if svc.packageKey %}
    <div class="sd-fact sd-fact--wide">
      <h3 class="sd-fact-h">In which packages</h3>
      {{ fitHas(svc.packageKey) }}
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if svc.callout %}
    <div class="sd-fact{% if not svc.packageKey %} sd-fact--wide{% endif %}">
      <h3 class="sd-fact-h">{{ svc.callout.title }}</h3>
      <p>{{ svc.callout.body }}</p>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</section>


{#- ══════════════ 3. HOW IT GETS MADE ══════════════ #}
{%- if not svc.noProcess %}
{%- set procWrap = "int-wrap" %}
{%- set processHeading = svc.processHeading or "How a project runs." %}
{% include "home/process.njk" %}
{%- endif %}


{#- ══════════════ 4. QUESTIONS ══════════════ #}
{%- if svc.faq %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <div class="sd-faq-grid">
    <h2 id="faq-h" class="int-h2">Questions</h2>
    <div class="sd-faq">
      {%- for item in svc.faq %}
      <details class="sd-q" name="faq"{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
        <div class="sd-a"><p>{{ item.a }}</p></div>
      </details>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}


{#- ══════════════ 5. OFTEN BOUGHT WITH THIS ══════════════ #}
{%- set rel = svc.related | resolve(services) %}
{%- if rel.length %}
<section class="int-wrap sd-sec" aria-labelledby="rel-h">
  <div class="sd-head">
    <h2 id="rel-h" class="int-h2">Often bought with this.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="sv-grid-wrap" data-spot=".sv-card">
    <ul class="sv-grid sd-rel" style="--cols: {{ rel.length }}">
      {%- for r in rel %}{{ card(r) }}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <span class="sv-spot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>
  <p class="sd-note"><a class="alv-tlink" href="/services/">Every service</a></p>
</section>
{%- endif %}


{#- ══════════════ 6. THE CLOSE ══════════════ #}
<section class="int-cta int-wrap">
  <span class="key-cone" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="key-pool" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {%- if svc.soon %}
  <h2 class="int-cta-h">Ask me where it stands.</h2>
  <p>Tell me what the business needs. I will say honestly when this opens, and what I can do for you today.</p>
  <div class="int-cta-act">
    <a class="alv-btn" href="/contact/">Start a project</a>
    <a class="alv-tlink" href="/services/">All services</a>
  </div>
  {%- else %}
  <h2 class="int-cta-h">Want this for your business?</h2>
